The layout sizes each computer from its real monitors: every window reports its displays (points on macOS, physical pixels on Windows, as the core sees them) to the server over the settings channel, and in its Bonjour record for a computer the server has not let in yet, so a computer appears with the right size when it is placed and follows monitors being plugged, unplugged or rearranged; the desktops beside it move along so they keep touching. Displays typed by hand stay until "Use them" picks up the reported ones.
